Rudroid Noncommercial Source-Share License
Version 1.0
Identifier: LicenseRef-Rudroid-NC-SourceShare-1.0

This is a custom noncommercial source-available license. It is not an
OSI-approved open-source license. It applies to Rudroid's first-party
material; identified third-party components retain their own licenses.

1. Definitions

"Licensor" means each copyright holder offering material under this
license. "You" means the individual or legal entity exercising a right
granted by this license. An entity's use includes use performed on its
behalf by its employees, contractors, or agents.

"Covered Work" means material expressly offered under this license and
your modifications, adaptations, and other copyright-derived versions
of that material. It includes source and compiled forms. It does not
automatically include independent works merely distributed alongside it,
independent guest programs or assets it loads, or outputs that contain
no copyright-protected material from the Covered Work.

"Commercial Use" means using, modifying, reproducing, distributing, or
providing the Covered Work in business operations or for revenue,
financial compensation, commercial advantage, or anticipated profit.
This includes selling or renting it; including it in paid hardware,
software, subscriptions, or services; commercial hosting or deployment;
advertising-funded or otherwise monetized services using it; and using
it to perform work for a business or paying customer. Making the Covered
Work available free of charge does not make an otherwise commercial
activity noncommercial.

"Corresponding Source" means the complete, preferred editable form of
the Covered Work needed to understand, modify, build, install, and run
the version you distribute or provide over a network. It includes all
your changes, required interface definitions, project-specific scripts,
build and installation instructions, and configuration templates. An
obfuscated, encrypted, incomplete, or machine-generated substitute for
the preferred editable source does not satisfy this definition.

Corresponding Source need not include personal data, credentials, signing
secrets, independent guest programs or assets, or ordinary unmodified
operating-system components, general-purpose tools, and independent
third-party dependencies obtainable separately. Identify necessary
dependencies and provide sufficient instructions to obtain and use them.
Excluding secrets does not excuse withholding implementation changes:
provide placeholders and configuration instructions instead.

2. Conditional copyright permission

Subject to every condition of this license, each Licensor grants you a
worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free permission to use, reproduce,
modify, and distribute its Covered Work solely for noncommercial
purposes. Personal study, hobby use, and research or education with no
commercial purpose are examples of permitted uses.

Commercial Use is prohibited. This license grants no commercial
permission, including for internal business use or paid deployment.
It does not grant rights a Licensor does not own or have authority to
license. Statutory rights that do not require the Licensor's permission,
including applicable fair-use rights, are not restricted by this license.

3. Same-license requirement

If you distribute a modified or other derived version of the Covered
Work, or allow third parties to use that version over a network, offer
the entire Covered Work in that version under this exact license.
Your own contributions to that version must carry the same grant and
conditions. Preserve the noncommercial restriction and the source-sharing
obligations. You may not replace them with a more permissive license or
add conditions that prevent recipients from exercising the permissions
this license grants.

This requirement applies to the Covered Work and your derived changes;
it does not relicense independent third-party material. You may not
distribute a combination whose other applicable terms make compliance
with this license impossible. Obtain compatible permission or exclude
the incompatible material before distributing the combination.

4. Public source when distributing

Whenever you distribute any Covered Work, including a modified version
or a compiled binary, make the Corresponding Source for that exact
version publicly downloadable under this license. Identify the matching
version or commit and provide a prominent source location with the
distribution. Providing only an upstream version that omits your changes
does not satisfy this condition.

The source must be available without a fee, registration requirement,
individual approval, or confidentiality obligation, in a commonly usable
format that recipients can retain. Include this license and all required
notices. Keep the source available while you distribute that version and
for at least three years after your last distribution of it.

5. Public source when providing network access

If you provide third parties with access to functionality of the Covered
Work over a network, provide a prominent, readily accessible link to the
Corresponding Source of the running version, including your changes.
The same publication, license, access, and retention conditions in
section 4 apply, with retention lasting at least three years after you
last provide access to that version.

This section does not authorize a commercial service. Commercial Use
remains prohibited even when all source is published. Private local
modifications that you neither distribute nor provide to third parties
over a network do not by themselves require publication.

6. Notices and identification

Preserve existing copyright, license, attribution, and disclaimer
notices in the Covered Work. Include this license and the project's
NOTICE file with source and binary distributions. Carry all lines
beginning "Required Notice:" into redistributed copies and their source
bundles. Mark modifications clearly and identify their authors and
matching source version. Do not imply endorsement by the original
authors or claim an official Rudroid release for your modified version.

No trademark rights are granted. Altering the license document or its
identifier does not change the terms governing material you received
under this license.

7. Limited patent permission

Each Licensor grants you a worldwide, nonexclusive, royalty-free patent
permission only for patent claims it controls that are necessarily
infringed by exercising the permissions expressly granted for its
contribution. This permission is limited to uses that comply with this
license. If you initiate a patent claim alleging that the Covered Work
or a contribution infringes a patent, this patent permission terminates
for you when that claim is initiated.

8. Contributions

When you knowingly submit original material for inclusion in a project
that identifies this license as its contribution policy, you offer that
material under this exact license. You must have authority to provide
the copyright and patent permissions involved. No copyright assignment
is implied. Identify third-party material and its actual license;
submission does not relicense it or cure an incompatibility.

9. Violations and termination

The permissions granted to you automatically terminate if you violate
these terms. If this is your first violation, you cease the violation,
and you fully correct it within 30 days after receiving written notice,
your permissions are reinstated unless the relevant Licensor informs
you otherwise in writing. Other reinstatement requires that Licensor's
written permission. Correction does not retroactively authorize a past
Commercial Use or waive claims arising from a violation.

Termination does not terminate the permissions of recipients who
independently comply with this license. Ending distribution or deleting
your copy does not remove the source-retention obligations already
incurred under sections 4 and 5.

